reduction: out[3] = sum of 32 terms, hand-built Low_level, 25 members
  01 serial                      [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 no schedule ops (the reference rendering)                              -> localized scope
  02 unroll-annot                [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll (annotated: codegen repeats the body)                           -> localized scope
  03 unroll-mat                  [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll ~materialize (the schedule mints the scope)                     -> localized scope
  04 unroll-outer-mat            [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll ~materialize of the OUTPUT axis                                 -> localized scope
  05 partition                   [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition of the reduction axis into three segments                    -> localized scope
  06 partition-then-unroll       [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition, then Unroll one segment (the seam stays addressable)        -> localized scope
  07 partition-outer             [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition of the OUTPUT axis (the reduction is inside a segment)       -> localized scope
  08 split-then-unroll           [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split the reduction axis, then Unroll ~materialize the inner half      -> localized scope
  09 split-then-swap             [f32         ] over plain                 Split the reduction axis, then Swap the halves                         -> localized scope
  10 pad-then-unroll-mat         [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Pad the reduction axis, then Unroll ~materialize (guarded copies)      -> localized scope
  11 split-reduce                [f32         ] over plain                 Split_reduce into four block partials plus a combine nest              -> scoped block partials + combine
  12 retype-vectorized           [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Vectorized                                -> SIMD accumulator grid
  13 split-then-vectorize-inner  [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split, then Retype the INNER half to Vectorized                        -> SIMD accumulator grid
  14 split-then-vectorize-narrow [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split into a two-wide inner half, then Retype it Vectorized            -> localized scope
  15 retype-workgroup-reduce     [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Workgroup_reduce                          -> warp-shuffle tree, or the localized scope where no lane index is bound
  16 retype-workgroup            [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Workgroup (no index bound: serialized)    -> localized scope
  17 runtime-guard               [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard, unscheduled                                    -> localized scope
  18 runtime-guard-unroll-mat    [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard under Unroll ~materialize                       -> localized scope
  19 runtime-guard-partition     [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard under Partition of the reduction axis           -> localized scope
  20 virtual-accumulator         [f32 bf16 f16] over virtual accumulator   a virtual accumulator inlined at its read site                         -> localized scope
  21 where-guarded-update        [f32 bf16 f16] over Where-guarded scope   virtualization's Where-guarded update spelling                         -> localized scope
  22 decline-data-guard          [f32 bf16 f16] over data-dependent guard  a data-dependent guard (not a pure index guard)                        -> per-step read-modify-write
  23 decline-sibling-statement   [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     a second statement in the reduction level                              -> per-step read-modify-write
  24 decline-sibling-unrolled    [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     the same level Unrolled: one read-modify-write per copy                -> per-step read-modify-write
  25 tile-mma-fallback           [f32 bf16    ] over small contraction     Tensorize whose emission preconditions fail (transposed-B operands)    -> Tile_mma scalar fallback
